{"licencia": {"dominios": ["classicapedia.com", "catdogpedia.com", "medicapedia.org", "mythicapedia.com", "culinapedia.com", "newtonpedia.com", "cinematopedia.com", "filopedia.com"], "ext": ["html", "htm", "js", "php", "json", "py", "txt"], "pares": [["creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/", "creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"], ["CC BY-NC 4.0", "CC BY-SA 4.0"]]}, "dia": [{"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "classicapedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "dia-personaje", "vacio": "", "texto": "<p class=\"dp-tag\">Personaje del día</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"dp-foto\" aria-label=\"Ampliar la foto\"><img src=\"r2/m/gustav-mahler.jpg\" alt=\"Gustav Mahler\" class=\"vz\"></button><h2><a href=\"b/gustav-mahler.html\">Gustav Mahler</a></h2><p class=\"dp-sub\">1860–1911 · compositor y director de orquesta austríaco de origen bohemio</p><p class=\"dp-txt\">Gustav Mahler (Kalischt, Bohemia, 1860 – Viena, 1911) fue un compositor y director de orquesta austriaco cuya obra sinfónica y de canciones, unida a una carrera al frente de algunos de los teatros más importantes de Europa, lo convierte en una de las figuras decisivas de la música culta…</p><a class=\"dp-leer\" href=\"b/gustav-mahler.html\">Leer la biografía →</a>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "classicapedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "hoy", "vacio": "", "texto": "27 de noviembre"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "classicapedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "efe-lista", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a class=\"efe p-medieval\" href=\"b/guillaume-du-fay.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1474</span><span><strong>Guillaume Du Fay</strong><em>Muere · compositor y teórico francés del siglo XV</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-siglo-xx\" href=\"b/arthur-honegger.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1955</span><span><strong>Arthur Honegger</strong><em>Muere · compositor suizo-francés</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-contemporaneo\" href=\"b/helmut-lachenmann.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1935</span><span><strong>Helmut Lachenmann</strong><em>Nace · compositor y pianista alemán</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-siglo-xx\" href=\"b/charles-koechlin.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1867</span><span><strong>Charles Koechlin</strong><em>Nace · compositor, profesor y musicólogo francés</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-barroco\" href=\"b/athanasius-kircher.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1680</span><span><strong>Athanasius Kircher</strong><em>Muere · polímata, teólogo y teórico de la música alemán, activo sobre todo en Italia</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-clasicismo\" href=\"b/francesco-bianchi.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1810</span><span><strong>Francesco Bianchi</strong><em>Muere · compositor italiano de óperas serias y cómicas</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-siglo-xx\" href=\"b/otto-kinkeldey.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1878</span><span><strong>Otto Kinkeldey</strong><em>Nace · musicólogo y bibliotecario estadounidense</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-romanticismo\" href=\"b/richard-mackenzie-bacon.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1844</span><span><strong>Richard Mackenzie Bacon</strong><em>Muere · periodista y escritor sobre música inglés</em></span></a>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "classicapedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "dia-personaje", "vacio": "", "texto": "<p class=\"dp-tag\">Figure of the day</p><button type=\"button\" class=\"dp-foto\" aria-label=\"Enlarge the photo\"><img src=\"../r2/m/gustav-mahler.jpg\" alt=\"Gustav Mahler\"></button><h2><a href=\"b/gustav-mahler.html\">Gustav Mahler</a></h2><p class=\"dp-sub\">1860–1911 · Austrian composer and conductor of Bohemian origin</p><p class=\"dp-txt\">Gustav Mahler (Kaliště, Bohemia, 1860 – Vienna, 1911) was one of the most important composers in European music at the close of the nineteenth century and the beginning of the twentieth. His symphonies and songs, many of them with orchestra, place him within the Austro-German tradition…</p><a class=\"dp-leer\" href=\"b/gustav-mahler.html\">Read the biography →</a>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "classicapedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "hoy", "vacio": "", "texto": "27 November"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "classicapedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "efe-lista", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a class=\"efe p-medieval\" href=\"b/guillaume-du-fay.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1474</span><span><strong>Guillaume Du Fay</strong><em>Died · French composer and music theorist of the fifteenth century</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-siglo-xx\" href=\"b/arthur-honegger.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1955</span><span><strong>Arthur Honegger</strong><em>Died · Swiss-French composer</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-contemporaneo\" href=\"b/helmut-lachenmann.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1935</span><span><strong>Helmut Lachenmann</strong><em>Born · German composer and pianist</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-siglo-xx\" href=\"b/charles-koechlin.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1867</span><span><strong>Charles Koechlin</strong><em>Born · French composer, teacher and musicologist</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-barroco\" href=\"b/athanasius-kircher.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1680</span><span><strong>Athanasius Kircher</strong><em>Died · polymath, theologian and music theorist, German by birth, active mainly in Italy</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-clasicismo\" href=\"b/francesco-bianchi.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1810</span><span><strong>Francesco Bianchi</strong><em>Died · Italian composer of serious and comic operas</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-siglo-xx\" href=\"b/otto-kinkeldey.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1878</span><span><strong>Otto Kinkeldey</strong><em>Born · American musicologist and librarian</em></span></a><a class=\"efe p-romanticismo\" href=\"b/richard-mackenzie-bacon.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1844</span><span><strong>Richard Mackenzie Bacon</strong><em>Died · journalist and writer on music</em></span></a>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "autor-hero", "vacio": "", "texto": "<div class=\"et\">Autor del día</div><img src=\"img/h/Q43216.jpg\" alt=\"Epicuro\" data-pie=\"Epicuro (341 a. C.–269 a. C.)\"><figcaption><h3><a href=\"a/epicuro.html\">Epicuro</a></h3><div class=\"f\">341 a. C.–269 a. C. · filósofo griego fundador del epicureísmo</div></figcaption>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "hoy", "vacio": "", "texto": "27 de noviembre"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "efe-lista", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/ada-lovelace.html\"><img src=\"img/r/Q7259.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1852</span><span><strong>Ada Lovelace</strong><em>Muere · matemática y escritora británica</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/eugene-o-neill.html\"><img src=\"img/r/Q93157.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1953</span><span><strong>Eugene O'Neill</strong><em>Muere · dramaturgo estadounidense</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/alejandro-dumas-hijo.html\"><img src=\"img/r/Q169150.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1895</span><span><strong>Alejandro Dumas hijo</strong><em>Muere · dramaturgo y novelista francés</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/han-kang.html\"><img src=\"img/r/Q5646626.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1970</span><span><strong>Han Kang</strong><em>Nace · novelista y poeta surcoreana, premio Nobel de Literatura 2024</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/emile-verhaeren.html\"><img src=\"img/r/Q193680.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1916</span><span><strong>Émile Verhaeren</strong><em>Muere · poeta belga en lengua francesa, crítico de arte y uno de los fundadores del simbolismo</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/atanasio-kircher.html\"><img src=\"img/r/Q76738.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1680</span><span><strong>Atanasio Kircher</strong><em>Muere · sacerdote jesuita y erudito alemán del Barroco</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/yeghishe-charents.html\"><img src=\"img/r/Q739413.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1937</span><span><strong>Yeghishe Charents</strong><em>Muere · poeta y narrador armenio</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/caroline-kennedy.html\"><img src=\"img/r/Q230303.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1957</span><span><strong>Caroline Kennedy</strong><em>Nace · abogada y diplomática estadounidense</em></span></a>"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "ancla": "id=\"idea-dia\"", "cerrar_ancla": true, "tras": "<h2>Idea del día</h2>", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><a href=\"a/diogenes-de-sinope.html\"><img class=\"curio-foto\" src=\"img/r/Q59180.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><p class=\"tag\"><a href=\"a/diogenes-de-sinope.html\">Diógenes de Sinope</a></p><p class=\"idea\"><strong>Naturaleza frente a convención</strong>lo correcto no depende de las costumbres, sino de lo que exige una vida acorde con la naturaleza humana.</p></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "ancla": "id=\"cita-dia\"", "cerrar_ancla": true, "tras": "<h2>Cita del día</h2>", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><a href=\"a/solon.html\"><img class=\"curio-foto\" src=\"img/r/Q133337.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><blockquote class=\"cita-dia\"><p>«Guarda todo con mesura.»</p></blockquote><p class=\"tag\"><a href=\"a/solon.html\">Solón</a></p></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "ancla": "id=\"curio-dia\"", "cerrar_ancla": true, "tras": "<h2>Curiosidad del día</h2>", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><a href=\"a/martin-lutero.html\"><img class=\"curio-foto\" src=\"img/r/Q9554.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><p class=\"tag\">Curiosidad · <a href=\"a/martin-lutero.html\">Martín Lutero</a></p><h3>Una promesa tras un rayo</h3><p>Según su propio relato, durante la tormenta de 1505 gritó: «¡Ayuda Santa Ana! ¡Me haré monje!». Después consideró aquel grito una promesa que no podía romper.</p></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "autor-hero", "vacio": "", "texto": "<div class=\"et\">Author of the day</div><img src=\"../img/h/Q43216.jpg\" alt=\"Epicurus\" data-pie=\"Epicurus (341 BC–269 BC)\"><figcaption><h3><a href=\"a/epicuro.html\">Epicurus</a></h3><div class=\"f\">341 BC–269 BC · Ancient Greek philosopher and founder of Epicureanism</div></figcaption>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "hoy", "vacio": "", "texto": "November 27"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "efe-lista", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/ada-lovelace.html\"><img src=\"../img/r/Q7259.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1852</span><span><strong>Ada Lovelace</strong><em>Dies · English mathematician and writer</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/eugene-o-neill.html\"><img src=\"../img/r/Q93157.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1953</span><span><strong>Eugene O'Neill</strong><em>Dies · American playwright</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/alejandro-dumas-hijo.html\"><img src=\"../img/r/Q169150.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1895</span><span><strong>Alexandre Dumas fils</strong><em>Dies · French playwright and novelist</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/han-kang.html\"><img src=\"../img/r/Q5646626.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1970</span><span><strong>Han Kang</strong><em>Born · South Korean novelist and poet, Nobel Prize in Literature 2024</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/emile-verhaeren.html\"><img src=\"../img/r/Q193680.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1916</span><span><strong>Emile Verhaeren</strong><em>Dies · Belgian poet and art critic who wrote in French, and one of the founders of Symbolism</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/atanasio-kircher.html\"><img src=\"../img/r/Q76738.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1680</span><span><strong>Athanasius Kircher</strong><em>Dies · Jesuit scholar and polymath of the Baroque era</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/yeghishe-charents.html\"><img src=\"../img/r/Q739413.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1937</span><span><strong>Yeghishe Charents</strong><em>Dies · Armenian poet and writer</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"a/caroline-kennedy.html\"><img src=\"../img/r/Q230303.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1957</span><span><strong>Caroline Kennedy</strong><em>Born · American lawyer and diplomat</em></span></a>"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "ancla": "id=\"idea-dia\"", "cerrar_ancla": true, "tras": "<h2>Idea of the day</h2>", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><a href=\"a/diogenes-de-sinope.html\"><img class=\"curio-foto\" src=\"../img/r/Q59180.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><p class=\"tag\"><a href=\"a/diogenes-de-sinope.html\">Diogenes of Sinope</a></p><p class=\"idea\"><strong>Nature versus convention</strong>what is right does not depend on custom but on what a life in accordance with human nature requires.</p></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "ancla": "id=\"cita-dia\"", "cerrar_ancla": true, "tras": "<h2>Quote of the day</h2>", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><a href=\"a/solon.html\"><img class=\"curio-foto\" src=\"../img/r/Q133337.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><blockquote class=\"cita-dia\"><p>“Nothing in excess.”</p></blockquote><p class=\"tag\"><a href=\"a/solon.html\">Solon</a></p></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "filopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "ancla": "id=\"curio-dia\"", "cerrar_ancla": true, "tras": "<h2>Curiosity of the day</h2>", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><a href=\"a/martin-lutero.html\"><img class=\"curio-foto\" src=\"../img/r/Q9554.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><p class=\"tag\">Curiosity · <a href=\"a/martin-lutero.html\">Martin Luther</a></p><h3>A promise after a lightning strike</h3><p>By his own account, during the storm of 1505 he cried out: “Help! Saint Anna, I will become a monk!” He later regarded that cry as a vow he could never break.</p></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "pinacopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "cuadro-hero", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a href=\"o/la-joven-de-la-perla-vermeer.html\"><img src=\"img/g/Q185372.jpg\" alt=\"La joven de la perla\"></a><figcaption><a href=\"o/la-joven-de-la-perla-vermeer.html\">La joven de la perla</a> · Johannes Vermeer</figcaption>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "pinacopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "hoy", "vacio": "", "texto": "27 de noviembre"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "pinacopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "efe-lista", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/bronzino.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1503</span><span><strong>Bronzino</strong><em>Nace · pintor manierista florentino, retratista de la corte de los Médici</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/william-orpen.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1878</span><span><strong>William Orpen</strong><em>Nace · pintor irlandés de retratos y pintor oficial de guerra británico</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/roger-de-la-fresnaye.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1925</span><span><strong>Roger de La Fresnaye</strong><em>Muere · pintor cubista francés</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/francisco-pacheco.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1644</span><span><strong>Francisco Pacheco</strong><em>Muere · pintor y tratadista manierista sevillano</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/magnus-enckell.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1925</span><span><strong>Magnus Enckell</strong><em>Muere · pintor simbolista finlandés</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/frank-dicksee.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1853</span><span><strong>Frank Dicksee</strong><em>Nace · pintor e ilustrador inglés de la época victoriana</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/bohumil-kubista.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1918</span><span><strong>Bohumil Kubišta</strong><em>Muere · pintor checo, a caballo entre expresionismo y cubismo</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/antonio-gisbert.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1901</span><span><strong>Antonio Gisbert</strong><em>Muere · pintor de historia español del siglo XIX</em></span></a>"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "pinacopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "ancla": "id=\"obra-dia\"", "cerrar_ancla": true, "tras": "<h2>Obra del día</h2>", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><a href=\"o/baco-enfermo-caravaggio.html\"><img src=\"img/g/Q2293936.jpg\" alt=\"Baco enfermo\"></a><h3><a href=\"o/baco-enfermo-caravaggio.html\">Baco enfermo</a></h3><p class=\"nota\">Caravaggio</p><p>Baco enfermo es uno de los primeros cuadros que se conservan de Caravaggio, pintado en torno a 1593-1594, cuando el artista acababa de instalarse en Roma tras dejar Milán. Se trata de un autorretrato disfrazado: el pintor se presenta como Baco, dios del vino…</p></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "pinacopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "ancla": "id=\"curio-dia\"", "cerrar_ancla": true, "tras": "<h2>Curiosidad del día</h2>", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><a href=\"b/pieter-de-hooch.html\"><img class=\"curio-foto\" src=\"img/r/Q314889.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><p class=\"tag\">Curiosidad · <a href=\"b/pieter-de-hooch.html\">Pieter de Hooch</a></p><h3>Un cuadro que llegó al Parlamento</h3><p>En 1916 la National Gallery de Londres adquirió una obra de De Hooch, A Musical Party in a Courtyard, y la compra provocó un debate en la Cámara de los Comunes que terminó con una censura a los fideicomisarios del museo. Una crítica publicada en The Burlington Magazine la calificó de cuadro pobre, obra de su periodo tardío y malo. El episodio muestra hasta qué punto su reputación dependía entonces de la fase en que se había pintado la obra.</p></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "pinacopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "cuadro-hero", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a href=\"o/la-joven-de-la-perla-vermeer.html\"><img src=\"../img/g/Q185372.jpg\" alt=\"Girl with a Pearl Earring\"></a><figcaption><a href=\"o/la-joven-de-la-perla-vermeer.html\">Girl with a Pearl Earring</a> · Johannes Vermeer</figcaption>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "pinacopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "hoy", "vacio": "", "texto": "November 27"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "pinacopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "efe-lista", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/bronzino.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1503</span><span><strong>Bronzino</strong><em>Born · Florentine Mannerist painter and court portraitist of the Medici</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/william-orpen.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1878</span><span><strong>William Orpen</strong><em>Born · Irish portrait painter and official British war artist</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/roger-de-la-fresnaye.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1925</span><span><strong>Roger de La Fresnaye</strong><em>Dies · Cubist painter from France</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/francisco-pacheco.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1644</span><span><strong>Francisco Pacheco</strong><em>Dies · Sevillian Mannerist painter and art theorist</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/magnus-enckell.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1925</span><span><strong>Magnus Enckell</strong><em>Dies · Finnish Symbolist painter</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/frank-dicksee.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1853</span><span><strong>Frank Bernard Dicksee</strong><em>Born · English Victorian painter and illustrator</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/bohumil-kubista.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1918</span><span><strong>Bohumil Kubišta</strong><em>Dies · Czech painter between Expressionism and Cubism</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"b/antonio-gisbert.html\"><span class=\"anyo\">1901</span><span><strong>Antonio Gisbert</strong><em>Dies · Spanish history painter of the nineteenth century</em></span></a>"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "pinacopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "ancla": "id=\"obra-dia\"", "cerrar_ancla": true, "tras": "<h2>Work of the day</h2>", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><a href=\"o/baco-enfermo-caravaggio.html\"><img src=\"../img/g/Q2293936.jpg\" alt=\"Self-Portrait as Bacchus\"></a><h3><a href=\"o/baco-enfermo-caravaggio.html\">Self-Portrait as Bacchus</a></h3><p class=\"nota\">Caravaggio</p><p>Sick Bacchus is one of the earliest surviving paintings by Caravaggio, usually dated to around 1593–1594, shortly after he had settled in Rome from his native Milan. It is a disguised self-portrait: the artist presents himself as Bacchus, the god of wine…</p></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "pinacopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "ancla": "id=\"curio-dia\"", "cerrar_ancla": true, "tras": "<h2>Curiosity of the day</h2>", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><a href=\"b/pieter-de-hooch.html\"><img class=\"curio-foto\" src=\"../img/r/Q314889.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><p class=\"tag\">Curiosity · <a href=\"b/pieter-de-hooch.html\">Pieter de Hooch</a></p><h3>A painting that reached Parliament</h3><p>In 1916 the National Gallery in London acquired a De Hooch, A Musical Party in a Courtyard, and the purchase caused a debate in the House of Commons that ended with a censure of the gallery's trustees. A critic in The Burlington Magazine called it a poor picture, a work of the painter's late and bad period. The episode shows how much his reputation depended on the phase in which a canvas had been painted.</p></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "culinapedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "efem", "vacio": "", "texto": "<p><span class=\"ef-n\">Nace</span> <a href=\"a/steven-silva.html\">Steven Silva (1986) · chef, actor y presentador filipino-estadounidense</a></p>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "culinapedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "curio", "vacio": "", "texto": "<b>Nombre inspirado en la música.</b> El nombre hace referencia al pop, el género musical dominante en los años setenta, cuando el plato fue bautizado. <a href=\"p/ayam-pop.html\">Ayam pop →</a>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "culinapedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "efem", "vacio": "", "texto": "<p><span class=\"ef-n\">Born</span> <a href=\"a/steven-silva.html\">Steven Silva (1986) · Filipino-American chef, actor and presenter</a></p>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "culinapedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "curio", "vacio": "", "texto": "<b>A name inspired by music.</b> The name refers to pop music, the dominant genre of the 1970s, when the dish was named. <a href=\"../en/p/ayam-pop.html\">Ayam pop →</a>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "medicapedia.org", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "medico-dia", "vacio": "", "texto": "<div class=\"marco\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Charles_Robert_Richet_nobel.jpg?width=500\" data-grande=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Charles_Robert_Richet_nobel.jpg?width=1280\" alt=\"Charles Richet\" data-pie=\"Charles Richet (1850–1935)\"></div><div><span class=\"et\">Médico del día</span><h2><a href=\"p/charles-richet.html\">Charles Richet</a></h2><p class=\"sub\">1850–1935 · médico y fisiólogo francés, premio Nobel por la anafilaxia</p><p>Charles Robert Richet (París, 1850-París, 1935) fue un médico y fisiólogo francés, profesor de fisiología en París y uno de los pioneros de la inmunología. En 1913 recibió el Premio Nobel de Fisiología o Medicina por sus trabajos sobre la anafilaxia, una reacción exagerada del organismo ante una…</p><a class=\"leer\" href=\"p/charles-richet.html\">Leer su historia →</a></div>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "medicapedia.org", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "curio-dia", "vacio": "", "texto": "<div class=\"num\">¿?</div><div><span class=\"et\">Curiosidad del día</span><br><b>Un nombre que distinguía enfermedades</b><p>En la Inglaterra del siglo XVI se empezó a usar el término smallpox para diferenciarla de la sífilis, que entonces se conocía como great pox, o 'gran viruela'. <a class=\"leer\" href=\"enf/viruela.html\">Viruela →</a></p></div>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "medicapedia.org", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "hoy", "vacio": "", "texto": "27 de noviembre"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "medicapedia.org", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "efe-lista", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/charles-scott-sherrington.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Prof._Charles_Scott_Sherrington.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1857</span><span><strong>Charles Scott Sherrington</strong><em>Nace · médico y neurofisiólogo británico, figura clave de la neurociencia moderna</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/david-bruce.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Davidbruce.JPG?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1931</span><span><strong>David Bruce</strong><em>Muere · médico y patólogo británico nacido en Australia, pionero en medicina tropical</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/johann-gottlob-leidenfrost.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Johann_Gottlob_Leidenfrost.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1715</span><span><strong>Johann Gottlob Leidenfrost</strong><em>Nace · médico, teólogo y físico alemán</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/edward-bach.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Dr_Edward_Bach_Oil_Painting.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1936</span><span><strong>Edward Bach</strong><em>Muere · médico, bacteriólogo y creador de las flores de Bach</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/fe-del-mundo.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/National_Scientist_Dr._Fe_Del_Mundo.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1911</span><span><strong>Fe del Mundo</strong><em>Nace · pediatra filipina, fundadora del primer hospital pediátrico de Filipinas</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/wilhelm-ebstein.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Wilhelm_Ebstein.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1836</span><span><strong>Wilhelm Ebstein</strong><em>Nace · médico alemán, impulsor de la dieta baja en carbohidratos para la obesidad</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/eugenia-sacerdote-de-lustig.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Eugenia_de_Lustig.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">2011</span><span><strong>Eugenia Sacerdote de Lustig</strong><em>Muere · médica ítalo-argentina, investigadora en cultivo de tejidos</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/honorio-delgado.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Honorio_Delgado.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1969</span><span><strong>Honorio Delgado</strong><em>Muere · psiquiatra, filósofo y educador peruano</em></span></a>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "medicapedia.org", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "medico-dia", "vacio": "", "texto": "<div class=\"marco\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Charles_Robert_Richet_nobel.jpg?width=500\" data-grande=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Charles_Robert_Richet_nobel.jpg?width=1280\" alt=\"Charles Richet\" data-pie=\"Charles Richet (1850–1935)\"></div><div><span class=\"et\">Physician of the day</span><h2><a href=\"p/charles-richet.html\">Charles Richet</a></h2><p class=\"sub\">1850–1935 · French physiologist and Nobel laureate for anaphylaxis</p><p>Charles Robert Richet (Paris, 1850 – Paris, 1935) was a French physiologist and physician, professor at the University of Paris and a pioneer of immunology. In 1913 he received the Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine for his work on anaphylaxis, an exaggerated reaction of the body to a foreign…</p><a class=\"leer\" href=\"p/charles-richet.html\">Read their story →</a></div>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "medicapedia.org", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "curio-dia", "vacio": "", "texto": "<div class=\"num\">¿?</div><div><span class=\"et\">Curiosity of the day</span><br><b>A name that set it apart</b><p>In 16th-century England the term smallpox began to be used to distinguish it from syphilis, which was then known as the great pox. <a class=\"leer\" href=\"enf/viruela.html\">Smallpox →</a></p></div>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "medicapedia.org", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "hoy", "vacio": "", "texto": "November 27"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "medicapedia.org", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "efe-lista", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/charles-scott-sherrington.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Prof._Charles_Scott_Sherrington.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1857</span><span><strong>Charles Scott Sherrington</strong><em>Born · British physician and neurophysiologist, a key figure in modern neuroscience</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/david-bruce.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Davidbruce.JPG?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1931</span><span><strong>David Bruce</strong><em>Dies · British pathologist born in Australia, a pioneer of tropical medicine</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/johann-gottlob-leidenfrost.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Johann_Gottlob_Leidenfrost.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1715</span><span><strong>Johann Gottlob Leidenfrost</strong><em>Born · German physician, theologian and physicist</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/edward-bach.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Dr_Edward_Bach_Oil_Painting.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1936</span><span><strong>Edward Bach</strong><em>Dies · physician, bacteriologist and creator of the Bach flower remedies</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/fe-del-mundo.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/National_Scientist_Dr._Fe_Del_Mundo.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1911</span><span><strong>Fe del Mundo</strong><em>Born · Filipino pediatrician who founded the first children's hospital in the Philippines</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/wilhelm-ebstein.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Wilhelm_Ebstein.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1836</span><span><strong>Wilhelm Ebstein</strong><em>Born · German physician who promoted a low-carbohydrate diet for obesity</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/eugenia-sacerdote-de-lustig.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Eugenia_de_Lustig.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">2011</span><span><strong>Eugenia Sacerdote de Lustig</strong><em>Dies · Italian-born Argentine physician and tissue culture researcher</em></span></a><a class=\"efe\" href=\"p/honorio-delgado.html\"><img src=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Honorio_Delgado.jpg?width=120\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"anyo\">1969</span><span><strong>Honorio Delgado</strong><em>Dies · Peruvian psychiatrist, philosopher and educator</em></span></a>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "mythicapedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "curio", "vacio": "", "texto": "<b>Una ruta italiana.</b> Durante un tiempo se pensó que la historia llegó a Rusia por fuentes italianas, aunque el origen más probable es el romance francés de Bevis de Hampton. <a href=\"d/bova-korolevich.html\">Bova Korolevich →</a>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "mythicapedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "curio", "vacio": "", "texto": "<b>An Italian route.</b> For some time it was thought that the story reached Russia through Italian sources, although the most likely origin is the French romance of Bevis of Hampton. <a href=\"../en/d/bova-korolevich.html\">Bova Korolevich →</a>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "ludicopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "dia", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a class=\"foto\" href=\"enciclopedia/pac-man.html\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"enciclopedia/img/480/pac-man-1.webp 480w, enciclopedia/img/pac-man-1.webp 900w\" sizes=\"(max-width:760px) 100vw, 55vw\"><img src=\"enciclopedia/img/pac-man-1.jpg\" alt=\"Máquina recreativa de Pac-Man\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture></a>\n      <div class=\"txt\"><span class=\"etq\">🕹️ Videojuegos clásicos · 1980</span><h3>🟡 Pac-Man y la edad de oro de los recreativos</h3><p>El videojuego de laberintos y fantasmas que llevó los recreativos a todo el mundo.</p>\n      <p class=\"cur\">💡 En 1999 el estadounidense Billy Mitchell logró la primera partida perfecta de Pac-Man: 3.333.360 puntos.</p>\n      <div class=\"botones\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"enciclopedia/pac-man.html\">📚 Leer su historia</a></div></div>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "ludicopedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "sabias", "vacio": "", "texto": "Con 64 discos, haciendo un movimiento por segundo, se tardaría unos 585.000 millones de años en terminar. <a href=\"enciclopedia/torres-de-hanoi.html\">Más sobre Torres de Hanói →</a>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "ludicopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "dia", "vacio": "", "texto": "<a class=\"foto\" href=\"encyclopedia/pac-man-arcade-golden-age.html\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/enciclopedia/img/480/pac-man-1.webp 480w, /enciclopedia/img/pac-man-1.webp 900w\" sizes=\"(max-width:760px) 100vw, 55vw\"><img src=\"/enciclopedia/img/pac-man-1.jpg\" alt=\"Pac-Man arcade machine\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture></a>\n      <div class=\"txt\"><span class=\"etq\">🕹️ Classic video games · 1980</span><h3>🟡 Pac-Man and the golden age of arcades</h3><p>The maze-and-ghosts video game that took arcades all over the world.</p>\n      <p class=\"cur\">💡 In 1999 the American Billy Mitchell played the first perfect game of Pac-Man: 3,333,360 points.</p>\n      <div class=\"botones\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"encyclopedia/pac-man-arcade-golden-age.html\">📚 Read its history</a></div></div>"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "ludicopedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "sabias", "vacio": "", "texto": "At the hardest level the elastic is raised to armpit or neck height, and only the best jumpers manage to hook it with a foot. <a href=\"encyclopedia/chinese-jump-rope.html\">More about Elastics (la goma) →</a>"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "tenispedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "ancla": "id=\"cdia\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><div class=\"curio\" data-n=\"Naomi Osaka Mascarillas con nombres\"><h3>Mascarillas con nombres</h3><p>En el US Open de 2020 jugó sus siete partidos con una mascarilla distinta, cada una con el nombre de una persona afroamericana asesinada en los últimos años.</p><p class=\"nota\">→ <a href=\"t/naomi-osaka.html\">Naomi Osaka</a></p></div></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "tenispedia.com", "archivo": "index.html", "id": "hoy", "vacio": "", "texto": "<div class=\"titulo-bloque\"><h2>Tal día como hoy · 27 de noviembre</h2></div><div class=\"hoy\"><div><h3>Nacieron un día como hoy</h3><ul class=\"hoy-p\"><li><img src=\"img/r/Q309395.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span><a href=\"t/radek-stepanek.html\">Radek Štěpánek</a><small>1978</small></span></li><li><img src=\"img/r/Q264212.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span><a href=\"t/raffaella-reggi.html\">Raffaella Reggi</a><small>1965</small></span></li><li><img src=\"img/r/Q357335.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span><a href=\"t/santiago-giraldo.html\">Santiago Giraldo</a><small>1987</small></span></li><li><img src=\"img/r/Q947368.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span><a href=\"t/joseph-walker-wear.html\">Joseph Walker Wear</a><small>1876</small></span></li><li><img src=\"img/r/Q3291257.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span><a href=\"t/mariana-simionescu.html\">Mariana Simionescu</a><small>1956</small></span></li><li><span class=\"sin\"></span><span><a href=\"t/joao-cunha-e-silva.html\">João Cunha-Silva</a><small>1967</small></span></li></ul></div><div><h3>Murieron un día como hoy</h3><ul class=\"hoy-p\"><li><img src=\"img/r/Q552646.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span><a href=\"t/philippe-washer.html\">Philippe Washer</a><small>2015</small></span></li><li><img src=\"img/r/Q11372588.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span><a href=\"t/lily-addison.html\">Lily Addison</a><small>1982</small></span></li></ul></div><div><h3>Este mes en la historia</h3><ul class=\"hoy-f\"><li><strong>1975</strong> · <a href=\"torneo/wta-finals.html\">WTA Finals</a> <small>(Individual femenino)</small><br><a href=\"t/chris-evert.html\">Chris Evert</a> ganó a <a href=\"t/martina-navratilova.html\">Martina Navratilova</a> <small>6–4, 6–2</small></li><li><strong>1979</strong> · <a href=\"torneo/paris-masters.html\">París-Bercy</a> <small>(Individual masculino)</small><br><a href=\"t/harold-solomon.html\">Harold Solomon</a> ganó a <a href=\"t/corrado-barazzutti.html\">Corrado Barazzutti</a> <small>6–3, 2–6, 6–3, 6–4</small></li><li><strong>1995</strong> · <a href=\"torneo/atp-finals.html\">ATP Finals</a> <small>(Individual masculino)</small><br><a href=\"t/boris-becker.html\">Boris Becker</a> ganó a <a href=\"t/michael-chang.html\">Michael Chang</a> <small>7–6, 6–0, 7–6</small></li><li><strong>1998</strong> · <a href=\"torneo/paris-masters.html\">París-Bercy</a> <small>(Individual masculino)</small><br><a href=\"t/greg-rusedski.html\">Greg Rusedski</a> ganó a <a href=\"t/pete-sampras.html\">Pete Sampras</a> <small>6–4, 7–6, 6–3</small></li></ul></div></div>"}, {"tipo": "insertar_tras", "dominio": "tenispedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "ancla": "id=\"cdia\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">", "texto": "<div data-respaldo style=\"display:contents\"><div class=\"curio\" data-n=\"Naomi Osaka Masks with names\"><h3>Masks with names</h3><p>At the 2020 US Open she wore a different mask in each of her seven matches, each bearing the name of a Black person killed in recent years.</p><p class=\"nota\">→ <a href=\"t/naomi-osaka.html\">Naomi Osaka</a></p></div></div>", "marca": "data-respaldo"}, {"tipo": "rellenar", "dominio": "tenispedia.com", "archivo": "en/index.html", "id": "hoy", "vacio": "", "texto": "<div class=\"titulo-bloque\"><h2>On this day · 27 November</h2></div><div class=\"hoy\"><div><h3>Born on this day</h3><ul class=\"hoy-p\"><li><img src=\"../img/r/Q309395.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span><a href=\"../en/t/radek-stepanek.html\">Radek Štěpánek</a><small>1978</small></span></li><li><img src=\"../img/r/Q264212.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span><a href=\"../en/t/raffaella-reggi.html\">Raffaella Reggi</a><small>1965</small></span></li><li><img src=\"../img/r/Q357335.webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><span><a href=\"../en/t/santiago-giraldo.html\">Santiago Giraldo</a><small>1987</small></span></li><li><i